{"author":{"id":"038d65070aa747b6bc9d50939fa697ec871a40ed259db54429b255bbef2581d6"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792795221,"nonce":"dLT8FirzZ+UmdB6NeuULkhV7msI=","title":"Synchronize shared files and versioned game assets through authorized R2 transfers","message":"Master roadmap: 455de32231e2b4a39765b4dff0223570b525ccec145049431e6483f5aa521f98\n\nMilestone: P1\n\nScope\nAdd explicit shared-root manifests and text/binary file discovery, immutable asset hashes/versions, scoped size-bounded upload/download, lazy retrieval and atomic disk writes. Support asset edit ownership/leases and conflict review for sprite/audio/binary files. Normalize paths and symlinks, exclude credentials/private files, handle file rename/delete, verify hashes and preserve unsaved local buffers. Store blobs externally and references in room state.\n\nAcceptance criteria\nTests cover interrupted/retried transfers, corrupt hashes, expired URLs, large assets, simultaneous edits, rename/delete and local dirty files. Shared roots cannot be escaped by traversal/symlink. Browsing/closing a room does not decode or retain the entire asset set. Storage quota and revocation enforcement hold for direct transfer URLs.\n\nAssociations and blocking dependencies are recorded below using full git-bug IDs. This issue remains open until implementation and validation are complete.","files":null}]}